#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b30ba91-ae46-5c8a-a706-eadf49473929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268294} {:answer/id #uuid "5487de66-7dc7-5034-8054-c95e685f72e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{4}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268295} {:answer/id #uuid "caf3373e-14ce-53af-958f-71db5e3cd93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268296} {:answer/id #uuid "b551016b-e3f4-554b-afb5-1871fb7b2e49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(x-3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268297} {:answer/id #uuid "39114682-6ec7-594e-8ef7-e381555c6285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caf3373e-14ce-53af-958f-71db5e3cd93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268296} :answer-field/id #uuid "22269ea3-ba61-5af1-b9c9-78ad9e0d52ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e23b9540-6b27-5f85-a262-32ee244fff8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-69751" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)} & =\\frac{A}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n12x+12=A(x-1)(x+5)+B(x-3)(x+5)+C(x-3)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(3)+12 & =A(3-1)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(3-3)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(3-3)(3-1) \\\\ 36+12 & =A(2)(8) \\\\ A & =\\frac{48}{16} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(1)+12 & =A(1-1)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(1-3)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(1-3)(1-1) \\\\ 12+12 & =B(-2)(6) \\\\ B & =\\frac{24}{-12} \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(-5)+12 & =A(-5-1)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(-5-3)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(-5-3)(-5-1) \\\\ -60+12 & =C(-8)(-6) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-48}{48} \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}=\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}.\n$$"}]}
